1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,599
Initially I thought I would need to put bias tape along the edge to prevent fraying.
最初我以为要沿边缘缝上包边带，防止散边。

2
00:00:03,599 --> 00:00:05,039
I've never used bias tape before.
我以前从来没用过包边带。

3
00:00:05,039 --> 00:00:09,680
In fact I had no idea what it was until the lady at my local fabric store suggested it to me one day.
事实上，我原本都不知道这是什么，直到有一天本地布店的女士推荐给我。

4
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:12,800
But because I've never used it I also have no idea how to attach it properly.
不过因为没用过，我也完全不知道怎样正确装上去。

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,800
I know google is free and youtube is right there but I've always preferred learning the hard way.
我知道网上搜索不用花钱，YouTube 就在那里，但我总是更喜欢用吃亏试错的方式学习。

6
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,760
So I just did what I thought would work which shocker it didn't.
所以我就做了自己以为可行的办法，结果，真“令人意外”啊，没成功。

7
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,960
The combination of me my machine and lace being really hard to control.
我、我的缝纫机，再加上特别难控制的蕾丝，这个组合。

8
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,279
Made me resort to handstitching the bias taping on.
让我最后只能改用手缝，把包边带缝上去。

9
00:00:25,279 --> 00:00:26,880
This was a colossal waste of time.
这完全是极大的时间浪费。

10
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:29,520
I realized in this whole process that the lace wasn't even fraying.
整个过程中我才发现，蕾丝甚至根本没有散边。

11
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,599
And that the bias tape wasn't the right shade of white.
而且包边带的白色也不是合适的那个色调。

12
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:34,709
So I instead decided to ditch that idea and just neaten up the edges.
所以我决定放弃那个想法，直接把边缘整理整齐。

13
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:37,120
After wasting about an hour on something I didn't even end up doing.
在一件最后根本没做成的事情上浪费了大约一小时后。

14
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,400
I moved on to the straps.
我接着开始处理肩带。

15
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,800
Really all I did was cut off the excess material that had originally been stitched into the seams of the pillowcase.
其实我只是剪掉多余材料，那些原本被缝在枕套的接缝里。

16
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,110
This upcycle was incredibly simple mostly because all of the hard work was already done for me.
这次改造非常简单，主要是因为困难的部分都已经有人替我完成了。

17
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,480
But that's the first one done the next piece seemed like a simple enough task.
第一件完成了。下一件看起来也是一项足够简单的任务。

18
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,159
I started with putting the top on and roughly pinning it where it needed to be taken in.
我先把上衣穿上，大致用别针标出需要收小的地方。

19
00:00:54,159 --> 00:00:58,400
Admittedly I probably could have done this more efficiently because I think I should have taken a little more off.
说实话，我大概可以做得更有效率，因为我觉得本来还该再收小一点。

20
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,520
But by the time I finished these clips I couldn't think of anything worse than touching my sewing machine at least for a few more days.
但拍完这些片段后，至少好几天里，我都想不出还有什么比再碰缝纫机更糟的事了。

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:06,960
Anyway I roughly pinned it and then sketched out a new outline with my chalk.
反正，我先大致别好，再用粉笔画出新的轮廓。

22
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:10,480
I really need better chalk for this task because this makes me want to rip my hair out.
做这事真的需要更好的划粉，因为现在这个每次都把我急得想抓狂。

23
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:14,399
Every single time if you guys know of a good quality chalk for fabric please do let me know.
每次都这样。如果你们知道质量好的布料划粉，请一定告诉我。

24
00:01:14,399 --> 00:01:17,599
I picked out my thread I had a perfect color match which is always satisfying.
我选了缝纫线，颜色完全匹配，总是让人很满足。

25
00:01:17,599 --> 00:01:19,990
This type of thread is another blessing from my great grandma.
这种线又是一份来自曾祖母的馈赠。

26
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,039
I don't really have to worry about buying new thread for every project which is great.
我基本不用为每个项目都买新线，这真不错。

27
00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:25,760
This flip was pretty simple and straightforward for the most part.
这个改造大部分时候挺简单、直接的。

28
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,640
I basically just did a zigzag stitch along the line I had drawn.
我基本就是沿着画好的线缝了一道之字形针迹。

29
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:32,640
And when I got to just before the waist I started folding the fabric to create the gathering I imagined.
快缝到腰部之前，我开始折布，做出自己想要的抽褶。

30
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,760
I saw a girl on tik tok doing this and I found it really satisfying to watch.
我在 TikTok 看到一个女孩这样做，觉得看着特别解压。

31
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,680
So naturally I had to try it for myself.
所以当然得自己试试看。

32
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:41,039
Unfortunately the footage for that part has vanished into thin air.
不幸的是，那部分素材凭空消失了。

33
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:43,510
So I'm really sorry but I have no way to show that part.
所以真的很抱歉，我没办法把那部分给你们看。

34
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,800
However it did end up working it's not as neat as I'd like for it to be.
不过最后确实成功了，只是没有我希望的那么整齐。

35
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,480
But that's just the perfectionist in me.
但那只是我内心的完美主义在作祟。

36
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:52,320
And now I know that I'm capable of doing this I fear no top in my wardrobe is safe.
现在知道自己能做到了，我怕衣柜里再没有一件上衣能“幸免”了。

37
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,839
Like I mentioned earlier this scarf is beautiful but it's offensively sheer.
就像前面说的，这条围巾很美，但薄得实在太透了。

38
00:01:55,839 --> 00:01:59,120
And I genuinely started off having no real clue what to pull together for this one.
刚开始，我真的完全不知道这件要拼出什么造型。

39
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,480
I almost gave up entirely.
我差点就彻底放弃了。

40
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:03,760
I designed a couple different things when trying out different necklines like this mini dress.
尝试不同领口时，我设计了几个方案，比如这条迷你连衣裙。

41
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:06,719
But I knew immediately that it was probably outside my realm of expertise.
但我立刻就知道，那大概超出了我的能力范围。

42
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:09,440
And I also was unlikely to wear it even if I was successful.
而且就算做成功，我大概也不太会穿。

43
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:14,000
It wasn't until I folded the material in half and tested what it would look like as a halterneck that it clicked for me.
直到把布对折，试了试挂脖款的样子，我才一下子想通。

44
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,990
So the design I ended up settling on is basically what I wanted originally but in top form.
所以最后定下的设计，基本还是最初想要的，只是变成了上衣。

45
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,320
Which if I'm honest I'll likely wear more often anyway.
说实话，这样我本来也更可能经常穿。

46
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:23,839
This whole process of trying to drape things directly on my body has made me realize.
这整个直接在自己身上试着垂坠布料的过程，让我意识到……

47
00:02:23,839 --> 00:02:26,560
How desperately I need to invest in a dress maker mannequin.
……自己有多需要买一个服装人台。

48
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:30,480
But I'm caught between buying that or an over locker and I'm really bad at making decisions.
但我在买人台和买包缝机之间犹豫，我真的很不擅长做决定。

49
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,800
Anyway at this point I was on my third upcycle of the day.
反正到这个时候，我已经在做当天的第三件改造了。

50
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,039
And I didn't have the patience to rethread my machine.
我已经没耐心给缝纫机重新穿线了。

51
00:02:35,039 --> 00:02:36,240
Also I had run out of bobbins.
而且我的梭芯也用完了。

52
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,640
And I couldn't be bothered unraveling one I already had.
我也懒得把已有的一个梭芯上的线拆掉。

53
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,120
So I just pretended like the purple thread was part of the vision.
所以我就假装紫色线也是设计构想的一部分。

54
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,960
The only seam I did on this was down the back.
这件我只在背后缝了一道接缝。

55
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,320
Initially the seam was dead straight.
一开始，那道缝线是完全笔直的。

56
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:48,719
Which I realized immediately after doing it that that kind of shape made no sense for the look I was going for.
刚缝好我就意识到，这种形状根本不符合我想要的效果。

57
00:02:48,719 --> 00:02:50,960
So I had to unpick it and redo it on an angle.
所以我得拆线，再斜着重新缝。

58
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:53,839
So that I could have that looser low back look I also realized.
这样才能做出更松弛的露背效果。我还发现……

59
00:02:53,839 --> 00:02:57,520
That the stitching was making the fabric bunch up which I'm assuming was an issue with my tension.
缝线让布料挤在一起，我猜应该是线张力有问题。

60
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,480
But I couldn't unpick and redo it again because the fabric was too delicate.
但我没法再拆线重缝一次，因为布料太娇贵了。

61
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,800
And I knew it would start to fall apart to be honest.
我知道它会开始散掉。说实话。

62
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,360
I wouldn't want anyone to look at this upcycle up close.
我可不想让谁近距离细看这个改造成品。

63
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:08,959
It's not my greatest work and that's partially because of my skill level but mostly.
这不是我最好的作品，部分是因为技术水平，但更多是……

64
00:03:08,959 --> 00:03:12,959
It's because of how impatient I became and I also lost motivation for this one.
……因为我越来越没耐心，而且对这件也失去了动力。

65
00:03:12,959 --> 00:03:15,560
Anyway that's everything from me here's the final results.
反正，我就说到这里。下面是最后的成果。
